hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-13 = cons "**Uncertainty is a number.** When graphs model incomplete knowledge, they attach probabilities or confidences, as" (cons "in probabilistic knowledge bases, embedding scores, and extraction pipelines with thresholds. The number" (cons "summarizes missing information without retaining it. Two facts at 0.8 confidence can't be composed into anything" (cons "well defined unless their sources are assumed independent, which is exactly what can't be checked once the reasons" (cons "are gone." (cons "" nil)))))
